if you allow it the Apple watch will  constantly pull you out of the real  world and suck you into your digital one  with constant chimes wrist vibrations  and pop-up alerts it can and it will  take over your life if you let it  that is after three weeks of wearing the  Apple watch I've learned how to tame it  turning it from an accessory of  distraction to a tool a real usefulness  here's how I did it the first thing I  did was use the Apple watch iPhone app  to limit notifications coming to my  wrist this is a must do if you want to  prevent it from becoming this an iPhone  handcuffed within the notification  settings in the iPhone app I turned off  the alerts for almost all third party  apps trivia crack notification should be  illegal in general and certainly on my  wrist with Apple's own apps I did a lot  of customization for instance the  calendar app only pings my wrist for  upcoming events now not new invitations  I'm also no longer buzzed to stand up  when I've been sitting for so long since  I was ignoring those anyway see I'm  standing in line for a hot dog  this may seem monotonous but do it it  will save you endless pestering later on  which brings me to my second step I set  up my watch to be a lot like a club  bouncer only allowing in VIP emails the  bad news here is that this only works  with Apple's Mail app still it was  really helpful since I get emailed day  in and day out about all sorts of things  I don't care about now only emails from  my editor and other important contacts  hit my wrist next I just flat-out killed  all the third party watch apps and  glances I'll never use I don't need all  those weather apps I have on my phone  and when am I going to need to check my  onedrive on my wrist I also switched off  the setting that automatically downloads  apps you have on your phone onto your  watch I also turned up the glances for  most apps including Apple Maps since  they aren't only distracting but very  slow to load the last thing I did was  find some wheel power to limit  distractions even further in those times  when you're with real people it isn't  always easy but turning on Apple's do  not disturb mode when sitting down with  a friend or a colleague is a must for me  I also embrace turning off the red  indicator on the watch face which tells  you if you have unseen notifications in  some cases it just became too addicted  and that's the interesting thing about  the Apple watch as technology becomes an  extension of our bodies it's on us as  well to limit its distractions  the Apple watch should bury us in the  digital world but help us in the real  one
 

